  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Wire Contour Passes tab now edits skim passes in cut order.\nEach skim offers a machine condition and a reverse toggle.\nUsers can add, remove and reorder skims.\nThe tab also exposes holding-tab count, width, positions and cut-off condition.\nUsers can declare that the freed piece is captured.\nApply uses the existing undoable EditOperationParams command.\nEffort: medium.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe project and command parameters already supported these values.\nThe operation page did not draw controls for them.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `wire_skims_add_reorder_remove_and_apply_undo`\n- `wire_tabs_and_capture_expose_all_stated_fields`\n- `wire_skim_apply_shows_each_named_refusal`\n- `wire_skim_limits_and_order_controls_disable_invalid_actions`\n- `wire_tab_position_limit_disables_add`\n- `wire_unknown_condition_ids_stay_visible_and_unchanged`\n\nThe initial three pins failed on the unchanged page because the controls were absent.\nRestoring upstream production made all six pins fail.\nRestoring the fix made all six pass.\nEnabling first-up, last-down, Add skim at the limit, or Add tab position at the limit made the corresponding pin fail.\nEach restoration passed.\nThe quick gate passed 807 tests with 5 ignored and no failures.\nClippy passed for camcraft-ui with all targets and warnings denied.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe .nc and .cl diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical wire EDM machine or pixel snapshots were exercised.\nNo generator or post code changed.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone.\nNo open PR touched the changed page or new test and decision files during the overlap check.\n\nChangelog: Add Wire Contour skim ordering, holding-tab fields and captured-piece controls to the Passes tab.\n\nFixes #1148\n",
